WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Open a packet of fish that isn't
fresh, and a sharp smell hits you.

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.640
The molecules behind it are amines:

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:11.600
ammonia with its hydrogen atoms
swapped for carbon groups.

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.340
Now squeeze a little lemon
juice over the fish.

5
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.000
The smell fades.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.480
So why does a squeeze of lemon
juice take the smell away?

7
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.060
In this mission, you'll meet
the amine family, primary,

8
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:26.540
secondary and tertiary, and see
how chemists classify them.

9
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.820
Then you'll make amines from
bromo compounds and nitriles,

10
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.460
and turn amines into amides.

11
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:38.110
Your mission: explain why a squeeze of
lemon juice takes the fishy smell away.